# T-1012: Single-scope Color type — verifies constructor injection and runtime output.
# Color: [type Red Green Blue] injects Red, Green, Blue as Variant(Color.Red, Null) etc.
# The TypeAlias entry (Color) is skipped at runtime — Color is NOT available as a
# runtime binding. result: Red uses the injected Red constructor directly.
# NOTE: Cross-scope TyCon identity rejection (two Color declarations in distinct nested
# scopes that should fail to unify) is NOT tested here — it is deferred to B-343
# (Arc<TyConDef> pointer-equality identity). Once B-343 lands a separate corpus test
# should verify that a value from an inner Color is rejected where an outer Color is expected.
[
  Color: [type Red Green Blue]
  result: Red
]
=== out
Dict({"Red": Variant(Color.Red, Null), "Green": Variant(Color.Green, Null), "Blue": Variant(Color.Blue, Null), "Color": Dict({"Red": Variant(Color.Red, Null), "Green": Variant(Color.Green, Null), "Blue": Variant(Color.Blue, Null)}), "result": Variant(Color.Red, Null)})
